==============================================================================
  2. Where the Stage-1 tokens go
==============================================================================
  corpus                   total    names   parens  literals  brackets   space
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------
  LOVABench v2               866      269      265       166         0     166
  algorithmic (Exp 12)       471      240      119        48        26      38
  apps/                      315      146       97        29        14      29

  On the algorithmic corpus, operator names and identifiers are
  51% of the cost and parentheses 25%.
  A new operator can only ever reclaim tokens from the *names*
  share, and only where it removes nesting.  The paren share is
  a property of s-expressions, not of the table.

  operator names costing more than one tiktoken token:
    0x0F mobius           2 tokens
    0x11 conserve         2 tokens
    0x17 violate          2 tokens
    0x18 surprise         2 tokens
    0x19 nil?             2 tokens
    0x1D trace-surprise   3 tokens
    0x1F deviation        2 tokens
    0x2A if-surprise      3 tokens
    0x2B loop-until       3 tokens

==============================================================================
  3. Three levers -- what each one is worth, and what it costs
==============================================================================
  task                       base  +alias  +prims  Python   contractions
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------
  factorial                    29      26      26      22   lt=0 sub=1
  fibonacci                    43      39      37      26   lt=1 sub=2
  is-prime                     84      74      69      56   lt=2 sub=0
  collatz-steps                70      63      63      51   lt=0 sub=0
  sum-to                       32      29      29      24   lt=0 sub=1
  power-of-two                 33      30      30      25   lt=0 sub=1
  gcd-euclid                   28      25      25      22   lt=0 sub=0
  count-divisors               68      61      59      31   lt=1 sub=0
  multiply-by-adding           36      33      33      28   lt=0 sub=1
  divide-by-subtracting        48      44      38      27   lt=1 sub=1
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------
  TOTAL                       471     424     409     312   lt=5 sub=7

  every column re-parsed and re-evaluated: 10/10 tasks, identical results
  (the `+prims` column was a projection when this experiment first
   ran; M10 shipped `lt` and `sub` as macros, so it now executes)

  lever                                   slots   tokens   vs Python
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  as shipped                                  0      471       0.66x
  + one-token operator aliases                0      424       0.74x
  + lt and sub (M10: macros, 0 slots)         0      409       0.76x

  gap to parity closed by the free lever:  30%
  gap to parity closed by the 2 slots:     9%

  node count (drives encoded bytes and the Stage-2 estimate):
    as shipped 330 -> with lt+sub 325 (2% fewer)

  `div` is not an idiom contraction -- it deletes a definition:
    today:        48 tokens, 33 nodes, O(a/b) recursion
    with a slot:  6 tokens, 3 nodes, O(1)
    One task's density, but every future program that divides.

  Residual after every lever: parentheses and identifiers, which
  no change to the table can reclaim.  Closing the rest means a
  different surface (Stage 2), not different operators.

==============================================================================
  4. Allocation ledger
==============================================================================
  free slots when this proposal was written: 14
  free slots now:                            8
    ['delta-check', 'respawn', 'budget-remaining', 'preserve', 'when-anomaly', 'predict', 'normal-range', 'par']
  (6 spent since -- see the M10 record in journal/README.md; the rows below are the proposal as measured, not the current state)

  proposed                        slots       basis
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------
  nil, cons, head, tail, nil?         5      census
                                                     one cons cell buys pairs AND lists AND strings-as-codepoint-lists; without it there is no two-value return and no collection at all
  div                                 1  complexity
                                                     48 tokens and O(a/b) recursion per use become 6 tokens and O(1)
  quote, eval                         2       axiom
                                                     a program as a value -- required by Axiom 1 and by Stage 3's (explain program), neither of which is reachable today
  lt, sub                             2     density
                                                     measured: 9% of the algorithmic density gap, 5+7 sites in 10 tasks
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------
  TOTAL                              10   of 14 free -> 4 slots headroom, deliberately unspent

  Not proposed:
    reallocate the number-theory family (8 slots)
      the census says 3-5% use outside the benchmark, which looks damning until you notice the demand above fits in 14 slots without touching it; spend them only if strings-as-lists proves too slow
    a dedicated string type (5-6 slots)
      unnecessary: a string is a list of codepoints once cons exists, and a "abc" surface literal is sugar, costing zero slots
    shorter operator names (0 slots)
      not a slot decision at all -- it is the single largest measured density lever and it is free; see the Axiom 8 revision

  What each lever is actually worth, side by side:
    lever                             slots   gap closed
    ----------------------------------------------------
    operator spelling (surface)           0         30%
    lt + sub (new primitives)             2          9%
    residual: parens + identifiers      n/a         61%

  The free lever is worth three times the two slots, and the
  residual is worth more than both together.  A table change
  is the wrong instrument for the density problem; it is the
  right instrument for the expressiveness problem.

